---
/** Source loader: paste a YouTube / MP4 / HLS link for both viewers, pick a local file, or load an HLS ladder from the private R2 bucket by its folder prefix. */
---

<div class="panel" style="margin-top:1rem">
  <h2>Play something</h2>
  <form class="row" id="source-form">
    <input class="field" id="source-input" placeholder="YouTube link, MP4 URL, or HLS master playlist (.m3u8)" autocomplete="off" />
    <button class="btn btn-brand" type="submit">Load for both</button>
    <button class="btn btn-ghost" id="pick-file" type="button">Use a local file…</button>
    <input class="hidden" type="file" id="file-input" accept="video/*,.mkv" />
  </form>
  <form class="row" id="hls-form" style="margin-top:0.75rem">
    <input class="field" id="hls-prefix-input" placeholder="R2 HLS folder, e.g. movie-hls (private bucket)" autocomplete="off" />
    <button class="btn btn-ghost" type="submit">Load R2 HLS for both</button>
  </form>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:0.75rem">
    <button class="btn btn-ghost" id="pick-upload" type="button">Upload a movie to the room…</button>
    <input class="hidden" type="file" id="upload-input" accept="video/mp4,video/webm,.m4v" />
  </div>
  <div id="upload-box" class="hidden" style="margin-top:0.75rem">
    <p class="hint" id="upload-label" style="margin:0 0 0.4rem">Uploading…</p>
    <div style="height:8px;border-radius:999px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.08);overflow:hidden">
      <div id="upload-fill" style="height:100%;width:0%;border-radius:999px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--amber,#EE8A1D),var(--ember,#D96A06));transition:width 0.2s ease"></div>
    </div>
    <button class="btn btn-ghost" id="upload-cancel" type="button" style="margin-top:0.5rem">Cancel upload</button>
  </div>
  <p class="hint">
    Upload sends the file from your browser straight into the room's private
    bucket (large files upload in pieces, so a shaky connection only retries
    the piece it dropped). When it finishes, the movie loads for both of you.
    Browser-playable files only: .mp4, .m4v, .webm, up to 5 GiB.
  </p>
  <section class="library" aria-labelledby="library-heading">
    <div class="row library-head">
      <h3 id="library-heading">Uploaded movies</h3>
      <button class="btn btn-ghost" id="refresh-library" type="button">Refresh</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hint" id="library-status">
      Join the room to see movies uploaded earlier. They remain reusable in
      new rooms until the bucket lifecycle removes them.
    </p>
    <div class="library-list" id="library-list"></div>
  </section>
  <p class="hint">
    HLS links adapt quality to each viewer's connection (great for R2-hosted movies — see
    <code>scripts/encode-hls.sh</code>). For a ladder in the <em>private</em> R2 bucket, use the
    R2 HLS folder field: the worker mints a signed playlist URL for room members only — a single
    presigned <code>master.m3u8</code> link cannot authorize the rendition playlists and segments
    under it. Local file: your partner must pick the <em>same file</em> on their device too — the
    file itself never travels, only play / pause / seek do.
  </p>
  <p class="error" id="source-error"></p>
</div>
